  - type: doi
    value: 10.5281/zenodo.20343439
    description: Zenodo archive of the released source code and assets
repository-code: "https://github.com/eygpcr/gpcr-sonification-beta2ar"
url: "https://github.com/eygpcr/gpcr-sonification-beta2ar"
abstract: >-
  An end-to-end open-source pipeline that maps activation-related
  geometric features extracted from G-protein-coupled receptor (GPCR)
  molecular dynamics (MD) trajectories onto musical parameters,
  renders the result as MIDI / WAV audio through multiple timbres,
  builds synchronised protein-cartoon videos and an interactive HTML
  player, and computationally validates information preservation by
  Random Forest cross-modal classification, leave-one-instrument-out
  generalisation, and canonical correlation analysis between the MD
  and audio feature spaces. The framework is system-agnostic and
  transfers to any GPCR (or any allosteric MD system) by adjusting
  the residue-selection strings only. We demonstrate it on three
  GPCRMD β2-adrenergic receptor reference trajectories spanning the
  activation continuum (inactive, active apo, active + orthosteric
  agonist) as a proof of concept.
keywords:
